{
  "title": "Pangea™ Partial Articular Proximal Tibia Plate",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/implants/423212/pangea-tm--partial-articular-proximal-tibia-plate",
  "subtitle": "Proximal Third Tibia Fracture Updated: Jun 8 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Related Implants",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea™ series contains 5 proximal tibia plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Extra Articular Proximal Tibia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Partial Articular Proximal Tibia (this topic)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Proximal Lateral Tibia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Proximal Posteromedial Tibia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Proximal Medial Tibia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Variable Angle Locking Technology**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423212/images/b78c9759-dea2-4e49-a0ac-c0621fc6540f_variable_angle.jpg",
              "caption": "Variable Angle"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Pangea’s variable angle locking technology uses a CoCr locking screw, which is harder than the Ti6Al4V ELI plate, allowing for the screwhead’s threads to form a definitive locking position in the plate’s locking hole by engaging the softer, Ti6Al4V ELI material.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "This technology allows the user to aim and lock the screw into the plate within a true 30° cone of the predetermined hole trajectory. The variable angle drill guide provided with the system offers guidance with respect to the limit of the 30° cone. The locking mechanism remains functional for up to three attempts at locking screw insertion.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Circular universal holes accept non-locking screws, and locking screws within a 30° cone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**2.0mm Proximal Suture Holes with Undercuts**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Allows for suture threading after plate placement and K-wire placement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423212/images/c342421d-2850-42ac-ad9c-c01165bd16be_screenshot_2025-01-08_at_10.47.13_am.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Proximal Row of Rafting Screws**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed to follow the angle of the tibial plateau to support the articular surface",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Locking or non-locking screws can be used to raft articular depression",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Window**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed to allow tamp placement for articular surface elevation and bone graft insertion after provisional plate application",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Oblong Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "To aid in plate placement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**2.0mm K-Wire Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "To provide temporary fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**2.2mm Plate Thickness**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed to increase patient comfort with a lower plate prominence designed to reduce potential for soft tissue irritation.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423212/images/c342421d-2850-42ac-ad9c-c01165bd16be_screenshot_2025-01-08_at_10.47.13_am.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Placement",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This plate is placed on the anterolateral surface of the proximal tibia",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "This plate is in proper position when the proximal end of the plate is adjacent to the articular surface allowing for the proximal screws to support the joint surface",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "This plate is in proper position when it can buttress the split lateral tibial plateau fracture",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fit",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The low profile (2.2mm) is designed to tightly contour to the shape of the proximal tibia with screw placement to allow buttress fixation of lateral split fragments",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Designed for treatment of Schatzker II fractures",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Under contoured to use the plate physically to provide buttress effect",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Proximal window for optional tamping, fracture visualization, and bone grafting after the plate is applied. Tamps are provided in Pangea instrument trays",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea Tibia Plating System is indicated for the internal fixation and stabilization of tibia bone fractures and osteotomies in normal and osteopenic bone, including:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Diaphyseal, metaphyseal, epiphyseal, extra- and intra-articular fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Non-unions, malunions, and deformities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Periprosthetic fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technical specifications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Standard plate lengths: 3-6 holes (85-127mm)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Thickness: 2.2mm",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Left and right anatomic plate options",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Drill bits: Ø2.5mm x 135mm (542020) Ø2.5mm x 215mm (542021)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
